10
00:55:52,941 --> 00:55:58,941
Won't You Be My Neighbor?

11
01:01:28,235 --> 01:01:34,235
is a 2018 American documentary film about the life and guiding philosophy of Fred Rogers, the
host and creator of Mister Rogers' Neighborhood, directed by Morgan Neville.

12
01:07:03,529 --> 01:07:09,529
The trailer for the film debuted on what would have been
Rogers' 90th birthday, March 20, 2018.

13
01:12:38,823 --> 01:12:44,823
The film premiered at the 2018 Sundance Film Festival and was
released in the United States on June 8, 2018.

14
01:18:14,117 --> 01:18:20,117
It received acclaim from critics and audiences and grossed over $22 million, becoming the top-grossing
biographical documentary ever produced and the 12th largest-grossing documentary ever produced.

15
01:23:49,411 --> 01:23:55,411
It was nominated for numerous awards, won the Independent Spirit Award for Best Documentary
Feature, and was chosen by Time magazine as one of its top ten films of 2018.

16
01:29:24,705 --> 01:29:30,705
The film explores themes of puppeteer, biography, based
on true story, childhood, puppet show.
